      },
      {
        "claim_id": "CC323_CARD_2",
        "text": "The review places Bitcoin's largest upward leg at 14:00-15:00 UTC (21:00-22:00 Bangkok).",
        "source_id": "SOURCE_1",
        "document_id": "cc323-midterm-lesson-20261106",
        "support_excerpt": "Our own dossier got the direction wrong for risk assets. DOS §6.1 mapped a Democratic sweep to US500 down, USTEC down and BTC down, following strategists (Hartnett, Yardeni). The sweep came, and those markets rose. The gold-up and USD-down legs were right.\n\nJim's question: when did each market move on 4 Nov?\n\nGold 05:00-07:00Z (12:00-14:00)\n\nUS500 04:00Z (11:00) A steady climb through Asia and Europe:\n\nBTC First leg 04:00-08:00Z Largest leg 14:00-15:00Z (21:00-22:00, US session)",
        "source_content_sha256": "b38301dfef9834244c0635590598ccf39e518af42a4dde5d21ea17e4400badde",
        "rights_class": "capital_chronicle_own_report",
        "rights_binding_sha256": "7a68c0985c4c136a1efe3a1977d88d56f3abc8dca204059495b97a39acd7f149",
        "publisher": "Capital Chronicle",
        "url": "urn:cc-public-report:main-retained:609d5443a5ec918426df4c0a8c79d2002d86348fa791250db085e3ba7c84d995"
      },
      {
        "claim_id": "CC323_CARD_3",
        "text": "The review says oil fell throughout the day, with its largest leg at 12:00-17:00 UTC (19:00-24:00 Bangkok).",
        "source_id": "SOURCE_1",
        "document_id": "cc323-midterm-lesson-20261106",
        "support_excerpt": "USOIL It fell all day. The largest leg was in the US session, 12:00-17:00Z (19:00-24:00)",
        "source_content_sha256": "b38301dfef9834244c0635590598ccf39e518af42a4dde5d21ea17e4400badde",
